# No em dashes

Never use em dashes (`—`) or en dashes (`–`) in anything we write or post (UI copy, emails, social captions, blog/video AI output, marketing templates, prompts that describe JSON field meanings for user-facing strings).

They read as AI-generated. Use commas, periods, colons, or a plain hyphen (`-`) instead.

Canonical helpers: `src/lib/text/humanize-copy.ts`
- Include `NO_EM_DASH_RULE` in AI prompts
- Run `stripEmDashes` / `stripEmDashesDeep` on model output before save or publish
